<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belaya (Kuban)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Belaya is a river of the north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, a left tributary of the Kuban about 270 kilometres long. It rises in the high mountains, cuts through deep gorges and flows past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maykop">Maykop</a>, the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adygea">Adygea</a>. Its valley was home to Circassian tribes such as the Abadzekhs, Temirgoy and Hatuqwai until the Russian conquest of the 1860s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belaya-river-kuban.jpg" alt="Belaya (Kuban)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yuriy75 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belaya_River_from_Rufabgo_bridge_002.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
